From: Tommy Huang <tommy_huang@aspeedtech.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Mar 2026 16:59:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6.12 1/1] i2c: ast2600: introduce buffer transferring support to AST2700

Upstream-Status: Backport [AspeedTech-BMC/linux aspeed-master-v6.12 a678e9cc4959a354a71e662d5dd25fab0da7fb7d, SDK v00.07.03]

Introduce buffer transfer behavior for AST2700 I2C controller

This patch add necessary logic and APIs to support buffer mode
operations on AST2700. The following features are implemented:

- Add transfer mode selection rules for AST2700.
- Implement ast2700_i2c_target_packet_buff_irq to handle
  buffer mode interrupt events.
- Add ast2700_i2c_setup_buff_rx() and ast2700_i2c_setup_buff_tx()
  to prepare RX and TX buffers for buffer mode transfers.

Signed-off-by: Tommy Huang <tommy_huang@aspeedtech.com>
Change-Id: Ib8dac79457dfc7e8218167fc323125871ae158b4
(cherry picked from commit f68df26148bd1f2d9af5cc79bf81aa2892727eab)

Taken from the Aspeed original, not the dgx/bmc/linux version: that one
carries [NvBMC] conflict resolutions against NVIDIA-only downstream code
(slave SW watchdog, tout-baseclk-div, disable-master, i2c_retries sysfs)
that the SONiC driver, plain Aspeed v00.07.02, does not have.
